    "body": "Yes it could be removed. However I do think there is value in writing down assumptions in the spec because it enables implementations to write `assert` statements, which 1) can help find bugs in specifications and 2) can help find bugs in the specification. Case in point most of my fixes to the spec have been found by stubbornly implementing any assertion in the spec text in my implementation and testing the code against html5lib-tests.",
